const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"订单类型也是时间选择",en:"Order type is also a timing choice"},body:{zh:"Foucault、Kadan与Kandel将限价单和市价单理解为对即时成交的不同需求。限价单可能改善价格，但需要等待且未必成交；市价单换取即时性。订单类型因而不能只用价格好坏判断，还应看到未成交和等待所带来的成本。",en:"Limit and market orders express different demands for immediacy. A limit order may improve price but must wait and may remain unfilled. Order choice therefore involves waiting and nonexecution, not just a comparison of quoted prices."},reference:{url:"https://www.edegan.com/pdfs/Foucault%20Kadan%20Kandel%20(2005)%20-%20Limit%20Order%20Book%20as%20a%20Market%20for%20Liquidity.pdf",label:{zh:"2005年期刊扫描版 · pp. 1171–1172",en:"2005 journal scan · pp. 1171–1172"}}},{title:{zh:"耐心是模型中的等待成本",en:"Patience means a cost of waiting"},body:{zh:"模型中的参与者都想完成单位交易，但等待成本不同。所谓有耐心与无耐心，是对这种成本的建模，不是对现实投资者性格或信息水平的标签。若用数据研究对应机制，应先说明怎样观察等待和订单选择，而不是直接猜测个人动机。",en:"Traders seek unit transactions but differ in waiting costs. Patient and impatient label these modeled costs, not personality or information quality. An empirical application must explain how waiting and order choices are observed rather than infer motives directly."},reference:{url:"https://www.edegan.com/pdfs/Foucault%20Kadan%20Kandel%20(2005)%20-%20Limit%20Order%20Book%20as%20a%20Market%20for%20Liquidity.pdf",label:{zh:"2005年期刊扫描版 · p. 1172",en:"2005 journal scan · p. 1172"}}},{title:{zh:"韧性有明确的事件边界",en:"Resiliency has an explicit event boundary"},body:{zh:"文章将韧性定义为流动性冲击后、下一笔成交前，价差恢复到原水平的概率。这与恢复所需秒数或价格反弹幅度不是同一个量。测量时若改变冲击、恢复目标或终止事件，就已经改变了指标，不能只保留相同名称。",en:"Resiliency is the probability that the spread returns to its former level before the next trade after a liquidity shock. It is not elapsed recovery time or a price rebound. Changing the shock, target or ending event changes the measure."},reference:{url:"https://www.edegan.com/pdfs/Foucault%20Kadan%20Kandel%20(2005)%20-%20Limit%20Order%20Book%20as%20a%20Market%20for%20Liquidity.pdf",label:{zh:"2005年期刊扫描版 · p. 1173",en:"2005 journal scan · p. 1173"}}},{title:{zh:"更多耐心交易者可能改变报价竞争",en:"Patient traders alter quote competition"},body:{zh:"在模型中，耐心交易者比例增加会改变流动性供需，并延长限价单的预期等待。提供流动性的人于是可能用更积极的报价缩短等待。这条机制将人群组成、订单选择与价差恢复连在一起，不能简化为交易数量越多市场就越好。",en:"A larger patient population changes liquidity demand and can lengthen expected waiting for limit orders. More aggressive quotes then help reduce waiting. The mechanism connects participant composition with recovery rather than equating more transactions with better markets."},reference:{url:"https://www.edegan.com/pdfs/Foucault%20Kadan%20Kandel%20(2005)%20-%20Limit%20Order%20Book%20as%20a%20Market%20for%20Liquidity.pdf",label:{zh:"2005年期刊扫描版 · p. 1173",en:"2005 journal scan · p. 1173"}}},{title:{zh:"到达更快不一定恢复更快",en:"Faster arrivals need not improve resiliency"},body:{zh:"更高的到达率缩短等待，可能让报价不必那么积极，因此价差恢复前需要更多订单。这里的结论对应论文的事件概率定义，不应改写成所有时间单位下恢复都更慢。阅读时必须同时保留模型机制和度量使用的时钟。",en:"Higher arrival rates shorten waiting and can reduce incentives for aggressive quotes, requiring more orders before recovery. This concerns the paper's event-probability definition, not every clock-time recovery measure. Preserve the mechanism and the measurement clock."},reference:{url:"https://www.edegan.com/pdfs/Foucault%20Kadan%20Kandel%20(2005)%20-%20Limit%20Order%20Book%20as%20a%20Market%20for%20Liquidity.pdf",label:{zh:"2005年期刊扫描版 · p. 1173",en:"2005 journal scan · p. 1173"}}},{title:{zh:"更小的报价单位并非单向改善",en:"A smaller tick is not a one-way improvement"},body:{zh:"文章说明，在某些以急于成交者为主的环境中，缩小最小报价单位可能削弱积极改善报价的动力，影响恢复并提高平均价差。这是均衡模型下的条件性结果，不是对某个交易所当前规则的结论，也不能单独支持一次具体制度变更。",en:"In some impatient-trader environments, a smaller tick weakens incentives to improve quotes, affecting recovery and average spreads. This is a conditional equilibrium result, not a diagnosis of a current exchange or sufficient support for a specific rule change."},reference:{url:"https://www.edegan.com/pdfs/Foucault%20Kadan%20Kandel%20(2005)%20-%20Limit%20Order%20Book%20as%20a%20Market%20for%20Liquidity.pdf",label:{zh:"2005年期刊扫描版 · p. 1173",en:"2005 journal scan · p. 1173"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"模型以等待成本不同的流动性交易者解释订单簿，不能把其中的交易选择直接当成知情交易识别。韧性采用特定概率定义，也不是所有市场恢复速度指标的同义词。",en:"The model explains liquidity trading through waiting costs, not identification of informed orders. Resiliency has a particular probability definition and is not interchangeable with every recovery-speed measure."}};export{e as default};
